<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African retail sales rise 2.7 pct m/m in March.</title>
<headline>S.African retail sales rise 2.7 pct m/m in March.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales rose a seasonally adjusted 2.7 percent month-on-month in March to 11.92 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 15.5 percent from 10.32 billion rand in March 1996, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were up 11.9 percent month-on-month and up 15.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				 Mar '97	 Feb '97	Mar '96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  11,918.4	11,605.6     10,317.8</p>
<p>    Actual		   11,302.2	10,096.0	9,818.8</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
